<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<model>
    <name>vacuum_dock</name>
    <version>1.0</version>
    <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
    <author>
        <name>Ilia O.</name>
        <email>iliao@kaia.ai</email>
    </author>
    <description>Auto-empty and mop-wash charging dock for oomwoo_one, 0.460 x 0.340 x 0.580 m, authored from primitives and built to avoid z-fighting: a 0.400 m wide core box, two 0.030 m side strips abutting it edge-to-edge, and four 0.015 m radius corner tubes whose diameter equals the strip thickness, so nothing overlaps on a shared flat plane. Strips and tubes run floor to top, so there is no seam between tower and bay walls. The drive-in bay is 0.400 wide (20 mm either side of the 0.359 m bumper), 0.240 deep and 0.170 high (73 mm over the 0.097 m turret). A 0.100 m spacer block closes the back of the bay, sized laterally to the core box, for charging contacts to be mounted on later. The bay carries NO collision geometry - only the core, side strips and spacer do - so the robot can sit in it without the physics ejecting it.</description>
</model>
